  "notes": "The source document (Exhibit XI.1, page 69) provides termination rates based solely on years of service, with no age dimension. The rates are constant across all ages for a given service duration. The target grid requires rates by age and service; since the source rates are age-invariant, the same service-based rate applies to every target age row. The source rates are printed as percentages (e.g., 2.00), so the 'values_unit': 'percent' flag is set to ensure the code rescales them to decimals (0.02). The 'overlap_weighted' operation is used for service bins where the target single year falls within a source range (e.g., target service 2 falls in source 2-8). For target service 1, it maps directly to source 1-1.99. For target service 30 and 40, they map to the '30 and over' bin which has a rate of 0.00. The target rows (ages) are irrelevant as the source has no age dimension; the same rate applies to all ages.",
